            {
              "id": "1ed17eb2-4e87-428d-889e-698cebc967ac",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Beyond Donkey Kong: A History of Nintendo Arcade Game</strong></em> was written by Ken Horowitz, published by McFarland, August 6, 2020."
            },
            {
              "id": "70aa3cfc-c55e-4ac5-be6e-9d074131a3e5",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "293b64ae-aa36-4c53-b05f-fd29a23885e3",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Before the enormously successful NES console changed the video game landscape in the 1980s, Nintendo became famous for producing legendary arcade machines like </em>Donkey Kong<em> and</em> Mario Bros.<em> Drawing on original interviews, news reports and other documents, this book traces Nintendo's rise from a small business that made playing cards to the top name in the arcade industry. Twenty-eight game titles are examined in-depth, along with the people and events that defined the company for more than four decades.</em>"
            }
          ]
        },
